# Line endings (V0.8.8). Without this, Git for Windows checks text files out
# with CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is its default), and a CRLF shell script or
# Caddyfile copied to the NAS/VPS breaks the containers ("no such file or
# directory" for a script that is plainly there). Force LF for everything
# that runs on Linux; keep CRLF for the Windows-only batch file.
*                text=auto eol=lf
*.sh             text eol=lf
Caddyfile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile*      text eol=lf
*.yml            text eol=lf
*.bat            text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.exe  binary
*.zip  binary
*.parquet binary
